# RESIZE while the subagents panel shows two live rows.
# testdata/faux/qa/resize-subagents.yaml dispatches two concurrent `task`
# calls and holds both replies behind a 3s delay so they are still
# "running" when the resize lands (see test/e2e/tui_gap_test.go's
# TestTUI_ResizeDuringLiveSubagentRow and testdata/faux/task_concurrent_tui.yaml
# for the fixture/pattern this is adapted from, driven there through the
# in-process PTY harness instead of a real terminal — that fixture's 400ms
# delay is far shorter than one real-terminal drive.py poll round-trip, so
# every observed run here found both subagents already finished by the
# time WAITFOR looked; see the qa yaml's own comment). --permission-mode
# dontAsk avoids an unrelated approval prompt for the `task` calls
# themselves, which is not what this scenario is about.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/resize-subagents.yaml
@fixture testdata/behaviour/qa/model-roles-fast-heavy
@size 120x40
@args --permission-mode bypassPermissions

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE dispatch two tasks
KEY enter
WAITFOR /2 subagents? running/ 20
SHOT subagents-running
EXPECT /look something up/
EXPECT /do the fast lookup/

# The 3s delay on both subagents' replies should still be running across
# a real window resize (~0.6s), but this SHOT is deliberately not gated on
# still being in the "running" state, only on not crashing — a slow
# driver round-trip could still land after both finish.
RESIZE 90 30
SHOT subagents-after-resize
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/

WAITFOR /2 subagents? finished/ 20
SHOT subagents-finished
EXPECT /2 subagents? finished/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
